      "content": {
        "heading": "5-Mark Board Question — Solved",
        "bullets": [
          "Q: Zinc granules + dilute H2SO4 → ? Write the equation + gas test",
          "Step 1: Zn + H2SO4 → ZnSO4 + H2 ↑",
          "Step 2: Burning matchstick → 'pop' confirms H2",
          "Trap: 'burns with a blue flame' instead of 'pop' = mark lost"
        ],
        "imageUrl": "/images/zinc_board_exam.jpg"
      },
      "teacherScript": "Time to earn five marks. This question has been repeated in multiple board exams. What happens when zinc granules are added to dilute sulphuric acid? Write the balanced equation, and describe how you would test the gas evolved. Step one: zinc displaces hydrogen, forming zinc sulphate and releasing hydrogen gas. Step two: bring a burning matchstick near the mouth of the test tube; the gas burns with a pop sound, confirming it is hydrogen. The trap: many students write, burns with a blue flame. Wrong. Hydrogen pops. And forget the balanced equation, and you lose a mark too. Write both, and the five marks are yours.",
